        },
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "Dilara.Atkins@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "Dilara.Atkins@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 30 2018 13:49:39 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-2-5em\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Not all cuffs</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-2-5em\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\">are created equal</span></span></span></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 30 2018 13:51:22 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,1)",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "Dilara.Atkins@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "Dilara.Atkins@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 30 2018 14:50:13 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\">Even pressure distribution</span></p>\n<p>Unlike other cuffs, our stiffener is RF-welded in place which delivers more consistent pressure distribution across the cuff’s entire surface, where as variations in high (red) and low (green) pressure leak paths can be seen with the competing cuff (as seen in Fig. A).<sup>1</sup></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Oct 31 2018 19:33:19 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text_2059127773": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "Dilara.Atkins@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "Dilara.Atkins@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 30 2018 14:51:03 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\">Optimizing occlusion</span></p>\n<p>Enables use of lower pressure settings; e.g., reaching a compression of 190 lbs ata pump pressure 45 mm-Hg lower than the competing cuff (as seen in Fig. B).<sup>1</sup></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Oct 31 2018 19:32:38 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
